{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1538433-101-outcast-famil","id":1538433,"title":"101 Outcast Famil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-11T08:33:57-07:00","id":1538433,"title":"101 Outcast Famil","content":"Wanted to brainstorm some possible homebrew family ideas for Outcasts (as well as others)<br /> <br /> Name of the game is to post a Family idea and continue the numbering on from the previous post/reply. Like so:<br /> 1. <b>Fae</b> - Outcasts that were exiled from the Outside by Fae Monarchs that rule in majestic Faelands. They like to form Bonds with Mortals by exchanging services, such as cleaning an apartment for food or giving the Mortal good luck in exchange for access to their Netflix account.<br /> 2. <b>Technolords</b> - Outcasts that are an amalgamation of circuitry and meat, there is a theory they left the Outside and merged with machinary when they arrived to Earth. They form Bonds with Mortals in digital spaces, sometimes offering friendship online in exchange for assisting their &quot;friend&quot; with digital issues. A fair number of influencers might have a Technolord patron on their Patreon manipulating the algorithm to boost their popularity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T14:38:56-07:00","id":1538494,"title":"","content":"Given how the theme of the Outcast curse is &quot;tried to rise beyond your station, was ironically gifted liminal mortality&quot;...<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Pardoners: </b>it's said the first Pardoner was a demonic torturer of the dead who rose up in anger at its master forbidding restorative justice. If she wanted to teach it a lesson, the Pardoners are glad to be the ultimate slow learners. Accusers and therapists both, Pardoners cultivate relationships with the despised, outcast, and criminal, and quietly judge if they can be guided back to the light...or are to be cut off from the body of society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T06:56:27-07:00","id":1540080,"title":"","content":"<b>4. The Timebound</b> - Outcasts from beyond the End of Time. The first of their kind entered open revolt against a being called Mother Epoch, trying to wrestle control of the flow of time from her, only to be hurled to the other side of Time itself. The Timebound are since trying to find a way back beyond that impossible frontier to travel and save themselves from the end of all things. They endure irreliable highs, as their optimism waxes and they believe they can change the course of events, followed by predictable lows as pessimism sets in and they feel the strings leading to Mother Epoch which make them danse to her tune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T20:31:54-07:00","id":1543604,"title":"","content":"After seeing the new Outcast manuscript, I feel really excited at the prospect of new Outcast families. Go here goes;<br /> <br /> <b>5 - The Scions</b>.<br /> Some creatures from the outside are not what we would call angels or demons, but perhaps resemble gods of myth and legend. The union of such being and humans creates a certain kind of Outcast - demigods or Scions as they call themselves. Scions are motivated to make names for themselves fulfilling some great purpose, essentially to be heroes. What form this heroism takes varies between individuals. Scions typically have great physical prowess and their magical ability is usually linked to that of their divine ancestor.<br /> <br /> <b>6. The Sycorax Family</b><br /> It is whispered that long ago, a witch served a powerful demon, perhaps even the Devil himself. They became lovers and she bore his monstrous offspring. This is a literal family descended from Sycorax, practicing her dark magic, engaging in incest to preserve the purity of their blood, and maintaining passing down their dark secrets. Ruthless and cruel, the Sycorax family crave power and dominance - both supernatural and temporal. They are often prone to madness or strange deformities, perhaps from their demonic ancestry or the inbreeding.<br /> <br /> <b>7. The Children of Night</b><br /> Descended from the unseelie fae of darkness and night, the Children of Night delight in the most frightening and macabre aspects of life. They dwell in the darkest remote forests, away from the prying eyes of mortals. They command the night itself, cold, darkness, and those creatures that dwell in it. Despite their frightening reputation, the Children if Night have a deep sense of honor and sometime use their powers to protect the innocent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 10-12-2024, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}